# Frontend evidence — interactive skill-activation UI (ADR 0021)

Scope: `apps/web-ui/` only (design/skills-ask-design.md Parts 5 and the
mid-flight Part 6 addendum). Backend endpoints (`POST
/api/v1/runs/{id}/skill-activation`, plus the six `/api/v1/skills*` CRUD
routes from Part 6) were implemented concurrently by a separate agent, in
the same tree; the two halves were not integration-tested against each
other end-to-end as part of this evidence (see "Honest limitations" below).

**Update, same session:** the design doc originally gave `SkillsSettings.tsx`
(list/install/activate/deactivate/policy) no backend to talk to. That gap
was flagged to the team lead instead of guessed at; the team lead closed it
with a Part 6 addendum specifying six `/api/v1/skills*` routes. This log now
covers both pieces — the inline ask/decide prompt (original scope) and the
Settings management panel (closed gap) — built in the same pass, once the
contract existed.

